        <cvss3_base_score>8.1</cvss3_base_score>
        <cvss3_vector>CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H</cvss3_vector>
        <synopsis>The file server accepts SMB version 1 and is missing a critical security fix.</synopsis>
        <description>The SMBv1 service mishandles crafted packets. An unauthenticated attacker on the network can run code on the device. This flaw has been used by self-spreading malware.</description>
        <solution>Apply the vendor firmware update and switch SMB version 1 off.</solution>
        <exploit_available>true</exploit_available>
        <plugin_output>The remote host answered an SMBv1 negotiation and is missing the fix.</plugin_output>
      </ReportItem>
